# Home manager — Caddy config to serve home.andrinoff.com over Tailscale
# (no public IP, no open ports) with a REAL, publicly-trusted cert.
#
# How it works:
#   1. DNS:  A record "home" -> your server's Tailscale IP (100.x.y.z),
#            proxy OFF (grey cloud). Tailscale IPs are only routable from
#            inside your tailnet, so the site is NOT exposed to the internet.
#   2. TLS:  Caddy issues a Let's Encrypt cert via Cloudflare's DNS-01
#            challenge (creates a TXT record), so it needs no inbound
#            port 80/443. The token only needs Zone:DNS:Edit permissions.
#
# The token is read from the CF_DNS_API_TOKEN environment variable. Set it in
# the caddy service (see setup-domain.sh) — do not hardcode secrets in files
# you commit.
#
# To run this:  sudo CF_DNS_API_TOKEN=<token> ./deploy/setup-domain.sh
# If no token is available, setup-domain.sh falls back to a local CA
# (tls internal) which requires trusting the CA once per device.
home.andrinoff.com {
	tls {
		dns cloudflare {env.CF_DNS_API_TOKEN}
	}

	encode zstd gzip

	handle_errors {
		@404 {
			path /api/*
		}
		respond @404 `{"error":"not found"}` 404
	}

	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
}
